# docker/plugins.manifest — curated XNAT plugins for the local dev/test stack.
#
# One entry per line; blank lines and #-comments are ignored. Staged by docker/stage-plugins.sh
# into docker/plugins/ (git-ignored), which docker-compose bind-mounts read-only into the
# container's ${xnat.home}/plugins. XNAT scans that dir once at boot, so after staging run
# `docker compose restart xnat` to load new/updated plugins.
#
# Entry forms:
#   source  <repo-dir> [git-ref]              build <repo-dir> with its gradlew xnatPluginJar, stage the -xpl jar.
#                                             If [git-ref] (branch/tag/commit) is given, the repo is checked out
#                                             to it first (refused if it has uncommitted changes).
#   file    <path-to-jar>                     stage an already-built jar as-is
#   coord   <group:artifact:version[:class]>  stage from Maven Local (~/.m2) — for published plugins
#
# Paths are relative to the xnat repo root. Keep this list curated and reviewed — every entry runs
# inside the XNAT container.

# Audit Trail Plugin — serves /REST/services/summary/audit/* (audit-trail screens + REST API,
# e.g. WorkflowSummaryTable). The jakarta / Restlet 2.6 / Turbine 7 migration lives on the
# feature/tomcat10 branch; it builds against org.nrg.xnat:web:1.11.0-SNAPSHOT (must be in Maven
# Local — see the xnat publish step).
source  ../audit_trail_plugin  feature/tomcat10
